  "caption": "$7.40 per GPU-hour: the median on-demand price of an NVIDIA B200 in our index, up 18% from $6.25 on 28 Oct.\n\nH100 ($3.90) and H200 ($4.80) also edged higher over the same weeks, while A100 ($1.75) and MI300X ($2.99) held flat.\n\nThe B200 range is wide: $3.69 at the low end, $16.11 at the high end. Against the H100, the median B200 hour costs about 1.9 times as much.\n\nData: Coloprice GPU index, 16 Nov 2026. Sources on the last slide.\n\nIs the Blackwell rental market tightening where you buy, or is this a mix effect? Tell us below. Full index: link in bio.",
